# Product stages and sources

This maintained reference follows sections 2, 3, and 5 of Product Documentation SOP, design baseline 0.2. The [Chinese export](阶段与来源.md) and its [provenance](阶段与来源.provenance.json) retain the original wording, source and export hashes, selected sections, and the identity of references omitted from the bundle. For current applicability, use the [common contract](共同约定.md) and the policy supplement (`.formsy-sop/skills/formsy-sop-workflow/references/sop-rules-addendum-20261016/applicability-and-version.md`).

## 2. Establish identity, sources, and status

### 2.1 Project and document identity

Maintain one identity record per project and update it across the four product stages.

| Field | Record | Completion condition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Project ID and name | Stable ID and a name the user recognizes | Link the project to its worktree, decisions, requirements, and artifacts. Use the project identity when locating files. |
| Product type and one-sentence goal | Who performs which task in which context and achieves which result | Express the user outcome. |
| Current stage and document version | Initialization, discovery, modeling, or planning, with the version ID | Give each revision a locatable version. |
| Prior-stage baseline | Stage version, decision ID, and original location, or none | Verify any effective prior confirmation required by the task. Record a blocker for dependent work if it is missing. |
| Target platforms and architecture | Platforms, architectures, version ranges, and specified installation or delivery form | Use effective user choices and record unresolved choices as pending. |
| Current scope | Included requirement, journey, and feature IDs, with explicit exclusions | Compare the documented set with all required objects. |
| Material and rule versions | Source snapshots and adoption records, PC and PM revisions, and applicable KB rule revisions | Preserve enough information to reproduce the review. Record any source change. |
| Document check, user confirmation, and actual test | Record ID, version, and status for each | Keep each result independently attributable. |
| Author, reviewer, and time | Human or model identity and version, relation to the author, and time zone | Attribute model review and any actual independent review accurately. |
| Open items, blockers, and next actions | Issue ID, affected scope, owner, and closure condition | Carry known material gaps across revisions. |

### 2.2 Sources, claims, and decisions

| Source ID | Identity and role | Original text and version location | Supported claim or object | Conditions and limits | Adoption record | Factual support |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
